**What was built** ΓÇö the `useVehicleCommand` web hook (1 mutation) ported to a UI-free KMP shared-core state holder:

- **`VehicleCommandModels.kt`** ΓÇö `CommandResult { success, message }` + `SendVehicleCommandInput { vehicleId, command, params? }`.
- **`VehicleCommandRepository`** (S7 port) + **`HttpVehicleCommandRepository`** ΓÇö `POST /vehicles/{id}/command` body `{ command, params }`; null `params` omitted (JSON.stringify parity). On 2xx it invalidates the four web `onSuccess` surfaces: `VehicleState[id]`, `Commands[latest:id]`, `Commands[history:id]`, and clears the `Vehicles` partition (`vehicleKeys.all`).
- **`VehicleCommandStore`** (S8) ΓÇö single suspend `sendCommand(): Result<CommandResult>`. Toast (render) and Tesla-auth-expired replay (platform recovery) are documented as out-of-scope; the failure flows out verbatim.
- **Tests** ΓÇö 6 contract tests (endpoint/method/body, params omit/present, success parse, eviction set, vehicle-scoped vs wholesale clear, failure-leaves-cache) + 4 store tests (input passthrough, success/failure passthrough). No non-trivial derivation ΓåÆ no golden vectors needed.

